And I'd love Dave, you know,
you're also in an organization,

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:23.470
I'd love to think about how
you personally are coping

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:26.480
and your organization, but, Asher Tosh,

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:28.840
you know, Khan Academy,
it's, this is a tarred time

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.853
for everyone, obviously.

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:34.500
Some of the good things that
Khan Academy had going forward

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:38.010
is we already had about
35% of our workforce,

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:40.350
was what we would say
remote or distributed.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:43.540
And so, we had a lot of
the infrastructure in place

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:47.230
where we could do meetings
over Google Hangouts or zoom.

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:49.770
We would use things like
Google docs to be able

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:52.770
to collaborate and so, that aspect of it

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:56.220
has been relatively okay for Khan Academy,

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:57.870
although it's still been difficult.

00:14:57.870 --> 00:14:59.810
I think the part that's been much harder

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:02.920
is now a lot of our team
